{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqpwne6dbsp","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Inject pipeline concurrency bottleneck diagnosis and batch ingest refactor design","summary":"Root cause of the daemon failing to bulk-ingest (it degraded /health at ~863 notes even client-throttled): three serial bottlenecks in POST /overlay/note (routes/overlay.js ~846). (1) Per note it does a pooled embed PLUS one embed per salient field (title, summary, each knowledge[] entry) PLUS optional source-cluster embeds — many embed round-trips per note. (2) All embeds funnel through a SINGLE MiniLM sidecar (lib/embed-server.js) exposing only POST /embed {text} — one text per call, no batching, single @xenova/transformers pipeline, so concurrent calls queue on one CPU/event loop. (3) A near-duplicate guard scans EVERY existing note computing cosine on each insert (overlay.js ~893) — O(n) per insert, O(n^2) across a bulk onboard, on the daemon main event loop. REFACTOR DESIGN (minimal, targeted at bulk onboard, low risk to the single-note hot path): (A) add POST /embed-batch {texts:[]} to embed-server.js calling _extractor(texts,{pooling:mean,normalize:true}) in ONE batched inference (transformers batches an array natively — far cheaper than N calls); (B) add embedBatch(texts) client in lib/embed.js; (C) add a bulk ingest route POST /overlay/notes/bulk {notes:[],workspace} that gathers all texts, embeds them in batches via embedBatch, SKIPS the O(n) dup-guard for bulk (known-distinct code symbols), writes all nodes, bumps epoch ONCE. Test approach: spawn a TEST embed-server on a temp socket to exercise /embed-batch and test bulk-route logic in-process; do NOT restart the production daemon/sidecar. Defer (separate, riskier): async-admit on the single-note path. This is the productized version of the cmm-onboard pipeline the bench validated.","category":"project","tags":["inject-pipeline","concurrency","embedding","refactor","bulk-ingest","daemon"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T0